  "text": "The woman at the well came for water and left a preacher. John chapter four. Jesus is tired from the journey and sits down by Jacob's well, and it is about the sixth hour, so around midday. A woman of Samaria comes to draw water, and he asks her for a drink. Which is already a scandal on two counts, because Jews had no dealings with Samaritans, and she says so to his face. Then the conversation turns. He offers her living water. She wants it. He says, go call thy husband. And she says, I have no husband. And he tells her, you have said well, for thou hast had five husbands, and he whom thou now hast is not thy husband. People often say she came at noon to avoid the gossip. That is a reasonable guess, and it is a guess. What the text actually says is that she left her waterpot, went back into the city, and said, come, see a man which told me all things that ever I did. And many of the Samaritans of that city believed on him because of her word. She dropped the jar and became the testimony.",
